IMPORT prelude

-- Pioneer Generation and Merdeka Generation Funds Act 2014 (Singapore) -- who is a Pioneer and who a Merdeka Generation Senior
-- (ss 12, 12A, 12B), loss of that status (s 18), the verification application to the Appeals Panel and its reconsideration (ss 13,
-- 14, 14A), which benefits go to which generation (s 16), protection of benefits from creditors (s 17(2)), recovery of overpayments
-- (s 22(1), (3)), use of confidential information (s 21), offences (s 23) and composition (s 25).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PGMGFA2014.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated
-- in the text is Act 31 of 2022 (wef 1 November 2022), to s 16(1)(a). The deposit's metadata calls it the current version as at
-- 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0075 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- SCOPED to status, verification, the menu of benefits and the rules that bite on recipients, providers and disbursers. Not encoded:
-- the Funds themselves (ss 4-11: establishment, purposes, expenses, withdrawals, financial year, accounts, audit, dissolution), the
-- Appeals Panel's constitution (s 15), the reimbursement grant to healthcare providers and its recovery (ss 16(2), 22(2)), the
-- disbursement machinery and information-sharing directions (ss 19, 20), offences by bodies corporate (s 24), service (s 26),
-- regulations (s 27, save the $2,500 / 6 months ceiling) and the validation provisions (ss 28, 29). THE AMOUNTS OF EVERY BENEFIT ARE
-- LEFT TO REGULATIONS ("of an amount prescribed"), WHICH WERE NOT RETRIEVED: this row says who may get what kind of benefit, never how
-- much.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pioneer Generation and Merdeka Generation Funds Act 2014 -- status and benefits`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The facts about a person, as they stand now. Birth year stands in for birthday: "31 December 1949 or earlier" is a birth year of
-- 1949 or before. "Continuously since" folds in the Act's "was a citizen of Singapore on [date] and has been a citizen of Singapore
-- since that date".
DECLARE Person HAS
    `birth year` IS A NUMBER
    `a citizen of Singapore now` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen continuously since 31 December 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen continuously since 31 December 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
    `determined a Pioneer by the Appeals Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `determined a Merdeka Generation Senior by the Appeals Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen of another country at any time after 9 March 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen of another country at any time after 26 June 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other citizenship arises only from Article 139` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dead` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared by the Minister to cease being a Pioneer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared by the Minister to cease being a Merdeka Generation Senior` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `12 and 18(1) -- Pioneers`

-- s 12(1): "a Pioneer is a citizen of Singapore -- (a) whose birthday is 31 December 1949 or earlier; and (b) who was a citizen of
-- Singapore on 31 December 1986 and has been a citizen of Singapore since that date." (2): "any other citizen of Singapore may be
-- determined under section 13 to be a Pioneer ... provided that the citizen's birthday is 31 December 1949 or earlier."
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Pioneer under section 12(1)` IF
        `the person`'s `a citizen of Singapore now`
    AND `the person`'s `birth year` AT MOST 1949
    AND `the person`'s `a citizen continuously since 31 December 1986`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be determined a Pioneer` IF
        `the person`'s `a citizen of Singapore now`
    AND `the person`'s `birth year` AT MOST 1949
    AND NOT `the person is a Pioneer under section 12(1)` `the person`

-- s 18(1): "an individual continues to be a Pioneer until -- (a) the individual ceases to be a citizen of Singapore at any time after
-- 9 March 2015; (b) the individual is or becomes a citizen of another country at any time after 9 March 2015, even if the individual
-- does not cease to be a citizen of Singapore; (c) the individual dies; or (d) the individual is declared under subsection (3) to
-- cease being a Pioneer." (3): the Minister may so declare "if the individual is convicted of an offence under this Act", after "a
-- reasonable opportunity of being heard" (4); the declaration "is final".
-- (5): "For the purposes of subsection (1)(b), an individual is not and does not become a citizen of another country by reason only
-- of the operation of Article 139 of the Constitution." -- subsection (1)(b) only: there is no such saving for subsection (2)(b).
-- (Ceasing to be a citizen is read here as no longer being a citizen now.)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has lost Pioneer status` IF
        (NOT `the person`'s `a citizen of Singapore now`)
    OR  (    `the person`'s `a citizen of another country at any time after 9 March 2015`
         AND (NOT `the person`'s `the other citizenship arises only from Article 139`))
    OR  `the person`'s `dead`
    OR  `the person`'s `declared by the Minister to cease being a Pioneer`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Pioneer` IF
        (    `the person is a Pioneer under section 12(1)` `the person`
         OR  `the person`'s `determined a Pioneer by the Appeals Panel`)
    AND (NOT `the person has lost Pioneer status` `the person`)

§§ `12A, 12B and 18(2) -- Merdeka Generation Seniors`

-- s 12A(1): a Merdeka Generation Senior is "(a) a citizen of Singapore -- (i) whose birthday is between 1 January 1950 and
-- 31 December 1959 (both dates inclusive); and (ii) who was a citizen of Singapore on 31 December 1996, and has been a citizen of
-- Singapore since that date; or (b) a citizen of Singapore -- (i) whose birthday is 31 December 1949 or earlier; (ii) [the same 1996
-- condition]; and (iii) who -- (A) is not a Pioneer; or (B) ceased being a Pioneer because of section 18(1)(d)".
-- (2): any other citizen may be determined under section 13 to be one if "(a) the citizen's birthday is 31 December 1959 or earlier;
-- and (b) the citizen -- (i) is not a Pioneer; or (ii) ceased being a Pioneer because of section 18(1)(d)".
-- "Is not a Pioneer" is read LITERALLY, as not a Pioneer now, whatever the reason. On that reading limb (B) adds nothing, since a
-- Pioneer declared under s 18(1)(d) is no longer a Pioneer. That limb (B) was written at all suggests the drafter may have meant
-- (A) more narrowly (never a Pioneer) -- an inference, not encoded.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Merdeka Generation Senior under section 12A(1)` IF
        `the person`'s `a citizen of Singapore now`
    AND `the person`'s `a citizen continuously since 31 December 1996`
    AND (    (`the person`'s `birth year` AT LEAST 1950 AND `the person`'s `birth year` AT MOST 1959)
         OR  (    `the person`'s `birth year` AT MOST 1949
              AND (    (NOT `the person is a Pioneer` `the person`)
                   OR  `the person`'s `declared by the Minister to cease being a Pioneer`)))

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be determined a Merdeka Generation Senior` IF
        `the person`'s `a citizen of Singapore now`
    AND `the person`'s `birth year` AT MOST 1959
    AND (    (NOT `the person is a Pioneer` `the person`)
         OR  `the person`'s `declared by the Minister to cease being a Pioneer`)
    AND (NOT `the person is a Merdeka Generation Senior under section 12A(1)` `the person`)

-- s 18(2): an individual continues to be a Merdeka Generation Senior until "(a) the individual ceases to be a citizen of Singapore
-- at any time after 26 June 2019; (b) the individual is or becomes a citizen of another country at any time after 26 June 2019, even
-- if the individual does not cease to be a citizen of Singapore; (c) the individual dies; (d) the individual is declared under
-- subsection (3) to cease being a Merdeka Generation Senior; or (e) the individual is determined under section 13(2) or 14 to be a
-- Pioneer." No Article 139 saving.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has lost Merdeka Generation Senior status` IF
        (NOT `the person`'s `a citizen of Singapore now`)
    OR  `the person`'s `a citizen of another country at any time after 26 June 2019`
    OR  `the person`'s `dead`
    OR  `the person`'s `declared by the Minister to cease being a Merdeka Generation Senior`
    OR  `the person`'s `determined a Pioneer by the Appeals Panel`

-- s 12B: "a citizen of Singapore may only be either a Pioneer or a Merdeka Generation Senior at any time, but not both." Encoded as a
-- condition on Merdeka Generation Senior status, since s 18(2)(e) shows the Pioneer status is the one that prevails.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a Merdeka Generation Senior` IF
        (    `the person is a Merdeka Generation Senior under section 12A(1)` `the person`
         OR  `the person`'s `determined a Merdeka Generation Senior by the Appeals Panel`)
    AND (NOT `the person has lost Merdeka Generation Senior status` `the person`)
    AND (NOT `the person is a Pioneer` `the person`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is both` IF
    `the person is a Pioneer` `the person` AND `the person is a Merdeka Generation Senior` `the person`

§§ `13, 14 and 14A -- verification by the Appeals Panel`

-- s 13(3): "A verification application may be made -- (a) by the individual ...; (b) with the approval of the individual, by another
-- person on behalf of that individual; or (c) where the individual is unable, by reason of physical or mental incapacity, to approve
-- a person to make the verification application, by a donee under a lasting power of attorney ... only to the extent permitted by
-- the Mental Capacity Act 2008."
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `another person with the individual's approval`
    `another person without the individual's approval`
    `a lasting power of attorney donee, the individual being incapable`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may make the verification application` IF
    CONSIDER `the applicant`
    WHEN `another person without the individual's approval` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 13(4): the application "must be made no later than" the closing date the Minister specifies, "and the Appeals Panel must reject
-- any verification application made after the applicable closing date". (5): the closing date is specified "by a notification in
-- the Gazette published at least 6 months before a closing date so specified". Dates are YYYYMMDD numbers.
GIVEN `received on` IS A NUMBER, `closing date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Appeals Panel must reject the application` IF
    `received on` GREATER THAN `closing date`

GIVEN `months between notification and closing date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the closing date is validly specified` IF
    `months between notification and closing date` AT LEAST 6

-- s 13(7) (and s 14(4)(a) on reconsideration): the Panel "may, where suitable, state that the citizen ... is a Pioneer or a
-- Merdeka Generation Senior ... with effect from a date before the date of its decision, but not a date earlier than when the
-- verification application (if made) for that citizen of Singapore was received by the Panel."
GIVEN `effective from` IS A NUMBER, `application received` IS A NUMBER, `decided on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the effective date is permitted` IF
    `effective from` AT LEAST `application received` AND `effective from` AT MOST `decided on`

-- s 14A(1): "Despite section 13(2)", where the Panel refused (or on reconsideration affirmed its refusal) to determine a citizen a
-- Pioneer, and "no application or further application under section 14(1) for reconsideration of that decision is received", the
-- Panel "may, on its own accord, decide whether that citizen may be determined a Merdeka Generation Senior if he or she is a citizen
-- of Singapore referred to in section 12A(2)". (2): no verification application is needed.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `refused as a Pioneer` IS A BOOLEAN, `reconsideration applied for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Appeals Panel may consider Merdeka Generation status on its own accord` IF
        `refused as a Pioneer`
    AND (NOT `reconsideration applied for`)
    AND `the person may be determined a Merdeka Generation Senior` `the person`

§§ `16 and 17 -- the benefits`

-- s 16(1): the financial assistance is "(a) a cash grant to be credited ... to the Medisave account or other account ... in the
-- Central Provident Fund"; "(b) for Pioneers only, a cash grant ... if he or she has any disability or satisfies such other
-- conditions as may be prescribed"; "(c) for Merdeka Generation Seniors only, a cash grant to be credited to the Merdeka Generation
-- Senior's PAssion Silver stored value card"; (d) a subsidy of premiums of a prescribed insurance scheme "in relation to health
-- services"; (e) a subsidy of premiums of a prescribed insurance scheme "in relation to any disability"; (f) a subsidy of the cost of
-- any relevant health service from a prescribed healthcare provider. Every amount is "prescribed".
-- (3): nothing "prevents a Pioneer or Merdeka Generation Senior from refusing any financial assistance".
-- s 17(1): "no Pioneer and no Merdeka Generation Senior has an absolute right to any financial assistance in section 16(1)".
-- s 27(3): "the means of a Pioneer or Merdeka Generation Senior are irrelevant" when prescribing the cash grants, the subsidy caps
-- and the reimbursement grant. The rule below is eligibility in kind, not entitlement.
DECLARE Generation IS ONE OF
    `Pioneer`
    `Merdeka Generation Senior`
    `neither`

DECLARE Benefit IS ONE OF
    `a Medisave cash grant`
    `a disability cash grant`
    `a PAssion Silver card top-up`
    `a health insurance premium subsidy`
    `a disability insurance premium subsidy`
    `a subsidy on a relevant health service`

GIVEN `the generation` IS A Generation, `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the benefit is of a kind section 16(1) offers` IF
    CONSIDER `the generation`
    WHEN `neither` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Pioneer` THEN
        CONSIDER `the benefit`
        WHEN `a PAssion Silver card top-up` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `Merdeka Generation Senior` THEN
        CONSIDER `the benefit`
        WHEN `a disability cash grant` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 17(2): the assistance "(a) is not assignable or transferable, except for the purpose of satisfying a debt due from the Pioneer or
-- Merdeka Generation Senior ... to the Government; and (b) is not liable to be attached, sequestered or levied upon for or in respect
-- of any debt or claim, except a debt due ... to the Government."
GIVEN `the debt is owed to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assistance may be attached for the debt` IF
    `the debt is owed to the Government`

§§ `22 -- recovery`

-- s 22(1): a cash grant or subsidy is "recoverable from the recipient as a debt due to the Government" where the recipient of a cash
-- grant "(i) is not a Pioneer or Merdeka Generation Senior ... or (ii) is ... but not eligible under this Act to that cash grant";
-- the recipient of a subsidy "is not eligible to the subsidy"; "(c) the amount paid is in excess of the amount the recipient is
-- eligible to receive"; or "(d) the money was paid, or was credited to a Medisave account ... in error".
-- (3): any person "(whether or not a Pioneer or Merdeka Generation Senior, or former ...)" who obtains assistance "by knowingly or
-- recklessly making any false or misleading statement" or by a document known to be false. s 23(5): prosecution does "not affect any
-- right to recovery under section 22".
GIVEN `the recipient has the status` IS A BOOLEAN, `eligible to that payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid in excess` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained by a knowing or reckless false statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is recoverable as a debt due to the Government` IF
        (NOT `the recipient has the status`)
    OR  (NOT `eligible to that payment`)
    OR  `paid in excess`
    OR  `paid in error`
    OR  `obtained by a knowing or reckless false statement`

§§ `21 -- confidential information`

-- s 21(2): use or disclosure of confidential information, "without the written consent of the individual to whom the information
-- relates, is authorised only if the purpose ... is to communicate or manage the confidential information as part of -- (a) the
-- funding, monitoring or evaluation (excluding the investigation into or resolution of complaints) of any health service, or of any
-- benefit under a prescribed public scheme ...; (b) the provision of indemnity cover ...; (c) the administration and enforcement of
-- this Act; (d) the prevention or management of a serious threat to public health or public safety; or (e) the development or
-- implementation ... of any public scheme involving benefits to Pioneers or Merdeka Generation Seniors."
-- (3): (2) does not authorise use "(a) in underwriting a contract of insurance that covers a healthcare provider ...; (b)
-- [deciding whether to insure one]; (c) [deciding whether a contract covers one in relation to a particular event]; or (d) in
-- employing a Pioneer or Merdeka Generation Senior."
-- (4): contravening (2) -- fine up to $5,000, imprisonment up to 12 months, or both.
-- With written consent (2) does not restrict the use at all; that (3) then does not bite either is an inference from (3) being
-- framed as a limit on (2).
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `monitoring a health service`
    `investigating a complaint about a health service`
    `providing indemnity cover`
    `administering and enforcing the Act`
    `managing a serious threat to public health`
    `developing a public scheme for the generations`
    `underwriting insurance for a healthcare provider`
    `deciding whether to employ the individual`
    `marketing to the individual`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is within section 21(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `monitoring a health service` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `providing indemnity cover` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `administering and enforcing the Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `managing a serious threat to public health` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `developing a public scheme for the generations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the individual consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 21(4)` IF
    (NOT `the individual consented in writing`) AND (NOT `the purpose is within section 21(2)` `the purpose`)

§§ `23, 25 and 27(4) -- offences and composition`

-- s 23(1): an offence where a person furnishes a document, statement or information to the Appeals Panel that "is false or
-- misleading, or ... omits any matter or thing without which the statement or information ... is misleading", the person "knows"
-- this, and it is "in, or in connection with, a verification application (whether for that person or for another)". (2): not an
-- offence if not false or misleading "in a material particular". Penalty: fine up to $5,000, imprisonment up to 12 months, or both
-- -- the same for s 23(3) (dishonestly obtaining assistance) and s 23(4) (a healthcare provider dishonestly obtaining a
-- reimbursement grant).
GIVEN `furnished to the Appeals Panel` IS A BOOLEAN, `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it` IS A BOOLEAN, `in connection with a verification application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an offence under section 23(1)` IF
        `furnished to the Appeals Panel`
    AND `false or misleading in a material particular`
    AND `knew it`
    AND `in connection with a verification application`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing confidential information`
    `a false statement to the Appeals Panel`
    `dishonestly obtaining assistance`
    `a provider dishonestly obtaining a reimbursement grant`
    `contravening the regulations`

-- s 27(4)(b): regulations may make a contravention "an offence punishable with a fine not exceeding $2,500 or with imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 6 months or with both" -- a ceiling for what the regulations may provide.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `contravening the regulations` THEN 2500
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `contravening the regulations` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 12

-- s 25(1): an authorised public officer may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $1,000."
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 1000
